    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0422" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg412"/>

                <head>Laird Brothers to her Majesty’s Treasury.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Birkenhead Iron Works,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Birkenhead,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 30, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> We received your telegram late yesterday
                    afternoon, as follows:</p>
                <p>“Captain Inglefield will, no doubt, in his dispositions regarding the iron-clad
                    vessels, take every proper precaution for the preservation of the property. The
                    orders have been well considered, and cannot be revoked or altered.”</p>
                <p>We take the liberty to draw the attention of her Majesty’s government to the
                    peculiar construction of the hulls and machinery of the vessels built by us <pb
                        facs="0423" n="413" xml:id="pg413"/> and seized by the government, and to
                    express to them our conviction that it is not possible, in their present
                    incomplete state, for any naval officer, by any dispositions he can make, to
                    protect the vessels from damage even in a dock, and much less in the open
                    roadstead of the Mersey, where, in our opinion, they cannot even be moored with
                    safety in this inclement season of the year.</p>
                <p>We are, sir, your obedient servants,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LAIRD BROTHERS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary to the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
